+at all depths and reports its exact Euclidean-remainder count.  A solver who
+uses the target depth and the proof invariant needs only three descent updates
+and two candidate gcds per row (240 high-level exact operations over 24 rows),
+but still has to carry out exact big-integer arithmetic without a tool.
+
+Construction and primality.  Factors are sampled before multiplication.
+For each row p=k*a^s+1 is accepted only with an executable Pocklington
+certificate: the fully factored part F=a^s of p-1 exceeds sqrt(p), and bases
+for every prime divisor of F pass Pocklington's congruence and gcd conditions.
+The smaller q is below 2^64 and is proved prime by the deterministic seven-base
+Miller--Rabin theorem for that range.  Thus every row really is a semiprime;
+probable primes are never silently used.
+
